it's hard to deny that we currently live  in a gta 5 gta online obsessed world the  games now spain across three console  generations and i'm honestly shocked  there hasn't been a port for switching  mobile yet don't even think about it  rockstar however no matter how many new  shiny versions of michael franklin and  trevor we get i'll still have a special  place in my heart for the man that came  before them gta 4's protagonist nico  bellick but what exactly is it about  nico that makes him stand out could it  be his sense of fashion his bowling  skills or maybe i just prefer playing as  one character in a gta game let's dive  deeper into who nico is and why he's  still a well-designed character 14 years  after he first toured through the  streets of liberty city  [Music]  everybody loves a good underdog story  right well when you break it down gta 4  is just that nico was born into a very  poor family and was forced to fight in  the yugoslav wars as a teenager he was  witness to many war crimes and most  likely committed some himself if that  wasn't enough he lost his second family  of sorts when most of his squad was  betrayed by one of their own being one  of only three survivors of the attack  nico became obsessed with finding the  traitor and getting revenge  i know the traitor was not me  so for ten years  i've been searching for the other two  one of them leaves here  why are you telling me this now do you  always get sentimental after you kill  people  you kept asking the poor guy was on a  steady losing streak that didn't get  much better after the war unable to find  a job nico fell into human trafficking  work in order to get by and i know i  know only a monster would smuggle and  sell other human beings so that last  point isn't really helping me sell him  as a great character but stick with me  because i believe that deep flaws like  that is what helped make nico more  believable we'll get to that in a second  following a bot's smuggling run neagle  joined the merchant navy to escape  russian crime boss ray balgren this in  turn led to his decision to head to  america where he thought he could start  fresh with his wealthy cousin roman in  reality roman was broker than the  district he lived in and america proved  to be just as crime infested as other  places in the world nico played the  cards he was dealt tried to reshuffle  but ended up with the same hand in a new  city rockstar made a deeply flawed  character with a troubled past and made  me believe that he was a guy down on his  luck looking for change i wanted so  badly for him to have at least one win  even if he technically didn't deserve it  because deep down we all want to believe  in second chances unfortunately for nico  that second chance was harder to achieve  thanks to three of his key motivating  factors money family slash loyalty and  revenge each time nico accepts a new  mission throughout the story one or more  of these factors lie behind his decision  to say yes and just like his flaws that  i hinted at earlier knowing nico's why  is another way that rockstar makes him  believable  a well-crafted character fits into their  story well leaving very little doubt in  the audience that they belong there nico  not only fits into liberty city but he  also feels very grounded in our real  world as well he's numb depressed angry  cynical and sarcastic he suffers from  ptsd and his worldview is based on all  of the horrors of his youth so you don't  question why he's agreeing to go against  standard morals you know his flaws and  motivation i believe that when nico  worked for vlad at the start of the game  because i knew that roman was in trouble  and nico was motivated by family and the  same goes for when niko ended vlad's  life he saw how the lone shark had  affected roman emotionally and wanted  revenge he had no problem pulling the  trigger because he felt his reason was  justified and being a bit numb from past  events murder doesn't have the same  effect on him as it does on roman who  rightfully freaks out the entire car  ride to vlad's fate it's depressing as  hell but it makes sense rockstar could  have made a crime game about a fish out  of water character adjusting to a new  city but instead they made nico an onion  with layers that are slowly peeled back  throughout the game his vulnerability  depth and backstory led me to believe  him more which led me to like him more  which led me to sympathizing with him  even though i've never experienced his  crime related struggles it also helps  that nico also showed more remorse at  times than some other characters we meet  throughout the game like in one  conversation when nego explained that he  wishes he could forget things he did in  the war and then immediately adds that  he wishes he could forget his actions in  liberty city as well or this scene with  faustin's wife that sealed the deal and  sold me on nico's inner conflicts life  is complicated i  i never thought i'd live like this  no when the war came i did bad things  after the war i thought nothing of doing  bad things  i killed people smuggled people  sold people  and you don't worry about your soul  after you walk into a village  and you see 50 children all sitting  neatly in a row against the church wall  each with their throats cut and their  hands chopped off  you realize that the creature that could  do this  doesn't have a soul nico seems to be a  neutral evil anti-hero and one way that  rockstar makes him easier to accept as  such is by having him follow his own  basic set of morals that other criminals  around him may not adhere to let's use  faustin for this example the man is an  unpredictable loose cannon that has no  code meanwhile nico has a method to his  madness he follows orders like he's been  trained to since he was young and seems  to need a good reason before killing  someone even if that reason is something  as small as an unpaid debt he goes  polite and kind to those who are the  same to him he says no to offers of  drugs and alcohol use and he isn't going  off on a rampage just for the hell of it  sure the game's open nature allows you  to take niko on killing sprees during  free roam but we're just talking about  the main story here the situations that  rockstar planned for nico to be in  everything adds up to a character that  feels genuine i still get the feeling  that nico is someone that i've bumped  into and luckily didn't get on the bad  side of as i roam the streets of new  york city throughout the years it also  helps that rockstar nailed the vibe of  manhattan and its surrounding barrels  gta 4 as a whole has a washed out color  palette and a gritty tone that makes it  feel like an nyc crime drama instead of  an overly satirical action-packed heist  flick nico never felt like a caricature  of an eastern european man and i think  that goes a long way to making him more  believable and well written  and finally i'm a huge sucker for  sarcasm and nico has a great dark  sarcastic humor i kick all the asses  that play me they call me the janitor  because you can't pay your debts and  they make you mop the floor  fertile man's cousin  what's your name again big mouth blick  very catchy sit down  may not be the best example of a great  human being but i think he's a great  example of a well-written character with  many layers rockstar was effective at  making the player care about him roof  for him but also hate him just enough so  that they don't feel like a horrible  human being themselves hit the comment  section let me know what you think about  nico or which gta character you think is  well written and why  [Music]
 

